by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-30T10:05:59Z

FTR, Console already sends OSC 9;4 from `ProgressBar` since #62112, and `QuestionHelper` pauses it while waiting for an answer. OSC 7501 would map well to that. A bar would report working with its percentage, a question would report blocked, and the exit code would give done or failed.

Why does Tui query for support first, BTW? 9;4 is sent blindly, and terminals usually ignore the OSC sequences they don't know. Outside `QuestionHelper`, Console can't read the reply to such a query, so sending blindly would be the only option there.

And the other way around: should Tui also send 9;4? Terminals that only know 9;4 would then show the progress of Tui apps.

